<newsitem itemid="41759" id="root" date="1996-09-09" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Nestor-BNA H1 result hit by disposal.</title>
<headline>Nestor-BNA H1 result hit by disposal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.10 loss	    vs 2.41 profit</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.27		   vs 1.15</p>
<p> Pretax		     5.9 loss	     vs 2.6  profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   64.9		   vs 58.6</p>
<p>NOTE - International healthcare group Nestor-BNA Plc said its restructuring is now complete and it has a strong base for future growth based on core operations. The first-half result was affected by a 9.2 million stg exceptional loss on the sale of its U.K. non-healthcare personnel businesses.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 3.3		    vs 2.9</p>
<p> Exceptional		9.2 loss	     vs nil</p>
<p> Interest (payable)     0.08		   vs 0.23</p>
<p> Tax			  0.9		    vs 0.8</p>
<p> Net taxed		  6.8 loss	     vs 1.8 loss</p>
<p> Retained		   7.8 loss	     vs 0.9 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   Oct 25</p>
<p>Div registration date  Sept 24</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
